Apple|apples]], chopped\n* ½ pound (225 g) [[Cookbook:Currant|currants]]\n* ½ pound (225 g) [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]], chopped\n* 1 glass rich, sweet [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* Fine [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Combine the suit, french roll, nutmeg, and lemon zest.\n#Mix in half a pound of apples, currants, raisins, stoned and chopped, wine, eggs, and a pinch of salt.\n#Mix all thoroughly together, and [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] it in a basin or mould for 3 hours.\n#Sift fine sugar over it when sent to table, and pour a white wine sauce into the dish.\n\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pudding]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon zest]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Windsor Pudding","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ pound (225 g) finely-shredded suet","sourceText":"½ pound (225 g) finely-shredded suet","amountText":"½ pound (225 g) finely-shredded suet","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"French roll","sourceText":"French roll","amountText":"French roll","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Small amount of ground nutmeg","sourceText":"Small amount of ground nutmeg","amountText":"Small amount of ground nutmeg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Lemon zest","sourceText":"Lemon zest","amountText":"Lemon zest","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ pound (225 g) apples, chopped","sourceText":"½ pound (225 g) apples, chopped","amountText":"½ pound (225 g) apples, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"½ pound (225 g) currants","sourceText":"½ pound (225 g) currants","amountText":"½ pound (225 g) currant